// Edge case: a value binder is checked against the outermost scope at its
// introduction, but it does not shadow. A parameter named `env` collides with
// the host module of that name and is reported -- and `env.get` inside the body
// still resolves to the host module, because the lowerer carries no value
// environment to bind the parameter in. The diagnostic exists precisely because
// the two disagree.
def lookup(env: Integer) -> F String {
  env.get("HOME")
}

//@ mode: lower-only
//@ expect: lowers
